        "doi": "10.1017/S001447972510015X",
        "label": "Montero-Sanchez et al. 2025",
        "limitation": "Gridded monthly weather and observational associations; farm management disease and tree competition remain relevant; pod counts are not traded tonnes",
        "mechanism": "Supports crop-stage lags and non-monotonic rainfall interpretation; does not establish a market signal",
        "source_url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/experimental-agriculture/article/effects-of-climate-and-withintree-competition-on-cocoa-pod-production-in-ghana/2F9415457E7C6E28FC01F050F4A7049D",
        "study_type": "Three-year repeated-observation farm panel"
      },
      {
        "doi": "10.1371/journal.pone.0200454",
        "label": "Gateau-Rey et al. 2018",
        "limitation": "Single Brazilian municipality near cocoa climatic limits; no untreated contemporaneous control; do not transfer the magnitude to West Africa",
        "mechanism": "Supports severe-drought tail-risk mechanism but not a West Africa effect size",
        "source_url": "https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0200454",
        "study_type": "Before-and-after natural drought study"
      }
    ],
    "record_count": 4,
    "selection_rationale": "The memo shows three near-term mechanism studies. The fourth registry record is a long-horizon suitability projection and remains context-only rather than being presented as evidence for a Dec-26 trade.",
    "translation_guardrails": [
      "Treat rainfall as non-monotonic: drought can damage cocoa, while excess rain and humidity can raise fungal-disease pressure.",
      "Apply crop-stage and lag logic; Ghana pod observations found strongest climate associations at fruit set with one-to-five-month lags by pod class.",
      "Do not transfer the magnitude of an extreme Bahia drought loss directly to Ghana or Cote d'Ivoire.",
      "Do not convert a grid-cell weather anomaly to production tonnes without crop-area weights, phenology, farm management, disease, and validated yield response.",
      "Observational and model-projection studies provide mechanism priors, not proof that a weather reading caused a market move or predicts returns."
    ]
  },
